Fix Neon connectivity failures and DB error handling

Three separate bugs made the storefront show an empty catalogue:

1. IPv6 black-hole. The network advertises IPv6 addresses that are not
   routable, so Node's happy-eyeballs selection latched onto them and every
   request timed out. .npmrc disables automatic family selection.

2. dbUnavailable() missed Neon errors. Neon wraps transport failures in
   error.sourceError, not error.cause, so the fallback never matched and the
   app threw a 500 instead of degrading. Now walks both plus own props.

3. Navbar called auth() unguarded. A DB blip took down every route because
   the navbar is in the root layout. Now returns a signed-out state.

Adds scripts/test-db-fallback.ts covering all four cases.